      description: "Methohexital is an ultrashort barbiturate anesthetic that rapidly produces hypnosis by enhancing GABA-A inhibition. Brain effect ends mainly through redistribution, so recovery can be quick after a bolus, but respiratory depression, hypotension, laryngospasm and repeated-dose accumulation remain possible. Unlike most anesthetics it can facilitate excitatory movement and is often selected for electroconvulsive therapy because it generally preserves seizure duration better than many alternatives.",
