      aliases: ["pancuronium bromide", "Pavulon", "aminosteroid paralytic"],
      brandExamples: ["Pavulon"],
      class: "Long-acting aminosteroid nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker with vagolytic effects",
      usedToTreat: "Longer skeletal-muscle paralysis for surgery or mechanical ventilation under general anesthesia/continuous sedation, analgesia, ventilation and quantitative neuromuscular monitoring.",
      description: "Pancuronium is a long-acting nondepolarizing paralytic that competitively blocks Nm nicotinic receptors. Its defining difference is cardiac muscarinic/vagal blockade and catecholamine effects that commonly increase heart rate, blood pressure and cardiac output. Significant renal elimination can make paralysis prolonged in kidney dysfunction. Like every paralytic, it has no effect on consciousness or pain.",
