      interactions: ["Succinylcholine increases malignant-hyperthermia risk in susceptible patients. Opioids, nitrous oxide and sedatives reduce MAC and compound respiratory depression. Sevoflurane potentiates nondepolarizing neuromuscular blockers. QT-prolonging drugs add repolarization risk."],
      keyLabs: ["Continuous end-tidal CO2, anesthetic concentration, ECG, blood pressure, oxygenation and temperature", "Potassium, ABG/VBG, lactate, creatine kinase, urine myoglobin and renal/coagulation studies if malignant hyperthermia is suspected", "Renal function when prolonged low-flow exposure raises Compound A concern"],
      nclexTraps: ["Sevoflurane is suitable for smooth inhaled induction because it is relatively nonpungent; that is not true of desflurane.", "Compound A risk is about absorber chemistry and exposure conditions, not an automatic kidney injury in every patient.", "Rising CO2 is an earlier malignant-hyperthermia clue than high temperature."],
