      usedToTreat: "Maintenance of general anesthesia and selected adult induction after airway planning; it is not used for pediatric inhaled induction and is poorly suited to smooth mask induction because it irritates the airway.",
      description: "Desflurane is a pungent volatile general anesthetic that suppresses cortical and spinal neural activity to produce unconsciousness and immobility; exceptionally low blood-gas solubility makes anesthetic-depth changes and emergence rapid. Its low boiling point requires a heated, pressurized agent-specific vaporizer. Pungency provokes coughing, breath-holding and laryngospasm, while rapid concentration increases can trigger sympathetic tachycardia and hypertension. It also carries the volatile-class malignant-hyperthermia, respiratory-depression and perioperative-hyperkalemia risks.",
